# P2P Contracts — Deployment Configuration Example
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (inside contracts/) and adjust if needed —
# the defaults below already match Stellar Testnet and this project's
# frontend config (see the root .env.example). `contracts/.env` is
# Git-ignored (see contracts/.gitignore).
#
# This file is consumed by contracts/scripts/deploy_testnet.sh, a
# plain shell script — not the Next.js app — so none of these need a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# IMPORTANT — NO SECRET KEY GOES IN THIS FILE, EVER.
# Deployment authenticates via the Stellar CLI's own local identity
# keystore (`stellar keys ...`), not a raw secret key in an env file.
# DEPLOYER_IDENTITY below is just the *name* of that local identity,
# not a secret. See contracts/scripts/deploy_testnet.sh's header
# comment for how to create one.

# Network to deploy to. This project uses Testnet through Level 5
# (see 00_MASTER_RULES.md #7).
STELLAR_NETWORK=testnet

# Soroban RPC endpoint for Testnet.
STELLAR_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org

# Testnet network passphrase (public, standard, same for everyone —
# not a secret). Matches NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE in
# the root .env.example.
STELLAR_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE="Test SDF Network ; September 2015"

# Name of a local Stellar CLI identity to deploy with (see
# `stellar keys --help`). This is a LABEL, not a secret — the actual
# key material lives in the Stellar CLI's own local keystore on your
# machine, never in this file or the repo.
DEPLOYER_IDENTITY=p2p-testnet-deployer

# --- eligibility_registry / loan_registry redeployment (POST-FCP-04) -------
# These are only needed for the init_eligibility_testnet.sh,
# allowlist_borrower_testnet.sh, and init_loan_registry_testnet.sh
# scripts — deploy_testnet.sh and deploy_eligibility_testnet.sh don't
# read any of these (they mint a brand new contract instance each run
# and print its ID for you to record here afterward).

# Local Stellar CLI identity that acts as admin for both
# eligibility_registry (allow-listing borrowers) and loan_registry
# (configuring its eligibility dependency). Optional — defaults to
# DEPLOYER_IDENTITY if unset. Set this separately only if you
# specifically want a different admin key than the deployer key.
#ADMIN_IDENTITY=p2p-testnet-deployer

# Contract ID printed by deploy_eligibility_testnet.sh. Required by
# init_eligibility_testnet.sh, allowlist_borrower_testnet.sh, and
# init_loan_registry_testnet.sh (which configures loan_registry to
# call this contract).
#ELIGIBILITY_REGISTRY_CONTRACT_ID=

# Contract ID printed by (re)running deploy_testnet.sh. Required by
# init_loan_registry_testnet.sh. This is deliberately separate from
# the frontend's NEXT_PUBLIC_LOAN_REGISTRY_CONTRACT_ID (see
# frontend/.env.example) even though they should end up holding the
# same value once redeployment is complete — this one is only read by
# the shell scripts in this directory.
#LOAN_REGISTRY_CONTRACT_ID=

# A borrower wallet address to allow-list by default when running
# allowlist_borrower_testnet.sh with no arguments (e.g. your own test
# wallet's public address, G...). A borrower address passed as a
# command-line argument to that script overrides this. Never put a
# secret key here — only ever a public G... address.
#TEST_BORROWER_ADDRESS=
